  "notes": [
    "Two tool systems: $1 = gang tool post + main spindle, $2 = back tool post + sub spindle. The X adds a Y2 axis so the back tool post can do off-centre / prismatic work on the sub spindle.",
    "Controlled axes: X1 Y1 Z1 C1 (gang / main), X2 Y2 Z2 C2 (back / sub).",
    "Sync: $-prefixed blocks select the active tool system. Line-up with '!' codes: !1L2 / !12L2 / !1!2L2. Queue / waiting M-codes are in the M600-M699 range.",
    "Sub-spindle synchronous rotation (pick-off): G814 / G114 engage spindle sync; G813 cancels. Superimposed / overlapping travel is used to shorten cycle time between the two systems.",
    "Back tool post: 4 modular + 4 stationary positions; more gang live-tool capacity than the VII (7 live spindles total).",
    "Guide bushing: SD125R standard; guide-bushing / non-GB switchable. Main spindle 200-15000 rpm, sub spindle to 12000 rpm."
